1
00:00:07,928 --> 00:00:13,047
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,369 --> 00:00:15,513
by Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki.

3
00:00:19,579 --> 00:00:25,281
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَامحمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

4
00:00:25,841 --> 00:00:30,903
 رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي۝وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي۝وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِيْ ۝يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِيِ۝

5
00:00:31,115 --> 00:00:39,164
We talked last evening about the covenant, this document that is drawn up by Rasool Allah ﷺ

6
00:00:39,496 --> 00:00:44,224
to govern the relationships of the different peoples of Madina.

7
00:00:44,722 --> 00:00:52,018
I've mentioned that you had Arabs who were polytheists and Muslims and then you have the Jewish tribes, of Madina.

8
00:00:53,165 --> 00:00:56,876
A few comments on the covenant, states the

9
00:00:57,662 --> 00:00:59,026
اُمَّهْ وَاحِدَّةْ دُوْنَ النَّاس

10
00:00:59,066 --> 00:01:00,347
It says that the believers are,

11
00:01:00,387 --> 00:01:02,460
أمة واحدة دون الناس,

12
00:01:02,974 --> 00:01:06,976
which is believers are allies to one another, excluding others.

13
00:01:07,549 --> 00:01:12,810
So, here you have the faith based community an Ummah(امة) established on faith,

14
00:01:12,882 --> 00:01:19,731
which was a novel concept to the Arabs who used to base everything on the relationship of blood.

15
00:01:20,035 --> 00:01:25,123
So now, Rasool Allah ﷺ is coming up with this concept of, "We are brothers because we are believers".

16
00:01:25,994 --> 00:01:31,628
And not only we are brothers, but we're brothers excluding everyone else,

17
00:01:31,653 --> 00:01:35,262
there's a special bond just because of us, being a Muslim.

18
00:01:35,471 --> 00:01:38,768
And that was a statement made in the document.

19
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:48,327
So, this might be one explanation of the reason, why you find that there were many orders, given by Rasool Allah ﷺ

20
00:01:48,515 --> 00:01:50,713
to distinguish the Muslims from the Jews, for example.

21
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:57,465
Now obviously, everything in Islam was distinguishing it, from the pagan worshipping, religion of Arabia.

22
00:01:57,996 --> 00:02:03,496
But since there are some commonalities between the Muslims and the People of the Scripture,

23
00:02:03,728 --> 00:02:06,657
Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't want that to overflow.

24
00:02:06,864 --> 00:02:10,729
He wanted the Muslims to keep a distinct identity.

25
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,220
So, you'd find that there are many Ahadith(احاديث)

26
00:02:13,458 --> 00:02:20,547
in which Rasool Allah ﷺ was ordering or instructing the Muslims to be different than the Jews of Madina.

27
00:02:21,149 --> 00:02:25,563
For example, you had the Jews of Madina did not pray in leather socks,

28
00:02:25,801 --> 00:02:26,985
so Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

29
00:02:27,047 --> 00:02:30,077
 صَلُّوْ بِالْخِفَافِ فَاِنَّ الْيَهُوْدَ لَا يُصَلُّوْنَ بِالْخِفَافْ

30
00:02:30,574 --> 00:02:34,141
The Yahood(يهود) of Madina would not dye with Hinnah(حنا),

31
00:02:34,181 --> 00:02:35,387
so Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

32
00:02:35,427 --> 00:02:36,883
 اُصْبُغوْا الشَيْب بالْحِنَّا

33
00:02:37,307 --> 00:02:40,425
 Dye your hair with Hinnah(حناء) and this is for men.

34
00:02:41,991 --> 00:02:48,174
When Rasool Allah ﷺ came into Madina, he saw that the Jews would fast on the 10th of Muharram(محرم), Aashoora(عاشوره),

35
00:02:48,214 --> 00:02:51,364
so he asked, he inquired for the reason.

36
00:02:51,778 --> 00:02:59,472
The response was that this was the day in which Allahسبحانه وتعالى saved Musa عليه السّلام from Firaun(فرعون).

37
00:03:00,059 --> 00:03:01,131
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

38
00:03:01,171 --> 00:03:03,742
 نَحْنُ اَوْلَآ بِمُوْسَى مِنْهُمْ

39
00:03:04,138 --> 00:03:07,921
Musa(موسى) belongs to us more than he belongs to them.

40
00:03:07,961 --> 00:03:12,532
Musa(موسى) was abeliever, so we are part of him and he is part of us.

41
00:03:13,326 --> 00:03:15,885
Therefore, we should fast on this day.

42
00:03:16,179 --> 00:03:21,861
And Rasool Allah ﷺ started the tradition of fasting on the 10th of Muharram(محرم), which is called Aashooraa(عاشوره).

43
00:03:22,363 --> 00:03:25,949
However, before he passed away ﷺ, he said;

44
00:03:26,147 --> 00:03:29,568
 لئن عشت إلى قابل لأصومن التاسع

45
00:03:29,838 --> 00:03:33,980
If I live until next year, I'm also going to fast the ninth of Muharram(محرم).

46
00:03:34,535 --> 00:03:38,080
So, rather than only fast the 10th, he was going to first the ninth and the 10th

47
00:03:38,136 --> 00:03:42,112
to distinguish the Muslims from the Jews, who would only fast the tenth.

48
00:03:44,008 --> 00:03:46,576
Second comment on this document.

49
00:03:47,338 --> 00:03:52,982
This document was establishing the authority of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who just walked in as a guest.

50
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:56,855
Rasool Allah ﷺ came into Madina, he was invited there.

51
00:03:57,567 --> 00:04:01,006
But Rasool Allah ﷺ was there to be followed.

52
00:04:01,339 --> 00:04:09,560
 وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَسُولٍ إِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۚ

53
00:04:10,122 --> 00:04:15,806
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that, any messenger that we send, We send them to be obeyed and followed.

54
00:04:16,328 --> 00:04:19,154
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was to be followed by the people.

55
00:04:19,413 --> 00:04:24,022
And he was establishing, his authority by the will of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, through various means.

56
00:04:24,102 --> 00:04:25,746
One of them was this covenant.

57
00:04:26,601 --> 00:04:33,111
By the way, the four projects that Rasool Allah ﷺ started with in Madina,

58
00:04:33,151 --> 00:04:35,611
I don't know, if I mentioned them before, but the four projects were;

59
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:36,746
Number one, the Masjid(مسجد)

60
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:41,232
that was number one, the first thing Rasool Allah ﷺ did when he wentinto Madina, was build the Masjid(مسجد).

61
00:04:41,872 --> 00:04:42,645
 Number two,

62
00:04:42,897 --> 00:04:45,743
establishing the Brotherhood between Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

63
00:04:46,059 --> 00:04:48,374
Number three, this covenant.

64
00:04:48,898 --> 00:04:52,517
Number four, the establishment of the Muslim army.

65
00:04:52,989 --> 00:04:59,317
All of these four were consolidating the foundations of this newly formed Islamic State,

66
00:04:59,801 --> 00:05:04,284
and it was consolidating the authority of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

67
00:05:04,577 --> 00:05:09,300
the one sent by Allahعَزّوجَلّ to bring the people out of darkness to light.

68
00:05:11,859 --> 00:05:13,737
So in the document, it says;

69
00:05:13,856 --> 00:05:21,472
وَاِنَّكُمْ مَااخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِيْهِ مِنْ شَئٍ فَاِنَّ مَرَدَّه’ اِلَى اللهِ ، وَاِلَى محمد

70
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:35,434
It says; Any matter in which you disagree, must be referred to Allah Al-Mighty and glorious is He and to Muhammadﷺ,

71
00:05:36,061 --> 00:05:41,004
 the only name mentioned in this document of an individual is that of Muhammadﷺ.

72
00:05:42,168 --> 00:05:48,049
Any matter of dispute that occurs between the Jews and the Arabs or the Arabs among themselves.

73
00:05:48,477 --> 00:05:53,232
Any matter of dispute that occurs between a citizen of Madina and an outsider,

74
00:05:53,549 --> 00:05:58,588
All of these matter, need to be referred to Allah and the Messenger of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

75
00:05:58,842 --> 00:06:02,096
So, this is establishing the rule of Allahعَزّوجَلّ in Madina,

76
00:06:02,826 --> 00:06:08,842
the governance of the book of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, and the Sunnah(سنة) of Muhammadﷺ.

77
00:06:09,879 --> 00:06:18,138
And this was agreed upon by everyone in Madina, the Muslims and the non Muslims, Arabs or Jews alike.

78
00:06:19,710 --> 00:06:20,750
Third comment,

79
00:06:21,234 --> 00:06:24,345
the relationship between the Muslims and the Jews.

80
00:06:24,894 --> 00:06:31,886
It is clear from this covenant that Rasool Allah ﷺ was extending ahand of tolerance towards the People of the Book.

81
00:06:32,968 --> 00:06:40,929
 You'd find that this document considers the Jews to be citizens of Madina, citizens of the Islamic State.

82
00:06:41,697 --> 00:06:45,379
They were granted religious freedom and state protection.

83
00:06:46,117 --> 00:06:49,607
They were allowed to worship according to their teachings.

84
00:06:49,813 --> 00:06:54,369
And number two, it was responsibility of the Muslim state to protect them.

85
00:06:55,193 --> 00:07:02,420
They were also required, on the other hand to support the Muslims against any enemy that attacke Madina.

86
00:07:02,770 --> 00:07:06,075
 They were also required to give sincere counsel to the Muslim state

87
00:07:06,099 --> 00:07:11,906
and never conspire against it, or to withhold information which was important to the security of the Muslim state.

88
00:07:12,433 --> 00:07:20,537
And also they were not allowed to leave from Madina without the permission of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

89
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:29,858
And they had to refer to Muhammadﷺ in any dispute that might arise between the Jews and the Muslims.

90
00:07:30,397 --> 00:07:31,696
So, this is how it started.

91
00:07:31,799 --> 00:07:34,728
This is how therelationship between the Muslims and the Jews started.

92
00:07:34,988 --> 00:07:38,545
However, from there on, it was always downhill.

93
00:07:38,871 --> 00:07:42,064
And the reason is, as we will see through these talks

94
00:07:42,317 --> 00:07:47,787
was the response of the Jews to the Muslim presence in Madina.

95
00:07:48,088 --> 00:07:52,251
But from the side of Rasool Allah ﷺ, this is how, he approached it,

96
00:07:52,652 --> 00:07:58,871
this is how he, dealt with the Yahood(يهود), in the early days of his immigration to Madina,

97
00:07:59,089 --> 00:08:05,278
he considered them to be citizens of the Islamic State, and he offered them protection and he gave them equal rights.

98
00:08:06,712 --> 00:08:10,656
The fourth comment establishing the sanctity of Madina.

99
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:17,663
Makkah was considered to be Haram(حرم) by the Arabs, Haram(حرم) is a sanctuary, it was Holy.

100
00:08:18,288 --> 00:08:20,854
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ is doing the same with Madina.

101
00:08:21,854 --> 00:08:23,100
It says in the document;

102
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:27,118
اِنَّ يَثْرِبْ حَرَامٌ جَوْفُهَا لِاَهْلِ هَذِہ الصَّحِيْفة

103
00:08:28,038 --> 00:08:35,103
The center of Yasrib(يثرب) is a sanctuary for everyone, in this covenant.

104
00:08:35,826 --> 00:08:40,080
And this includes not cutting down trees, they're not allowed to hunt,

105
00:08:40,795 --> 00:08:46,439
and they're not allowed to fight within the boundaries of this area or carry weapons.

106
00:08:47,367 --> 00:08:50,423
So, these are a few comments regarding this covenant.

107
00:08:51,755 --> 00:08:56,531
Some of the Sahabah, were held back from Hijrah(هجرة), so they came after Rasool Allah ﷺ,

108
00:08:56,556 --> 00:08:59,214
the majority made Hijrah(هجرة) before Rasool Allah ﷺ did,

109
00:08:59,730 --> 00:09:04,230
but some of them were held back such as Sohaib Ar-Roomiرضي الله عنه.

110
00:09:04,714 --> 00:09:11,277
Sohaib(صهيب), when he decided that he's going to leave Makkah, he had some wealth.

111
00:09:11,817 --> 00:09:18,164
 Sohaib Ar-Roomi(صهيب الرومي) was imprisoned by the Romans in one of the wars between the Romans and the Arabs,

112
00:09:18,299 --> 00:09:21,632
they took him as a prisoner and they enslaved him.

113
00:09:22,231 --> 00:09:26,672
So, he grew up among the Romans and he acquired their language.

114
00:09:27,172 --> 00:09:29,525
So, he had this accent when he would talk Arabic.

115
00:09:31,632 --> 00:09:36,798
And then he was sold from one owner to another, from one slavemaster to the next.

116
00:09:37,149 --> 00:09:39,439
And he ended up in the hands of Abdullah Bin Jada'an(عبدالله بن جدعان).

117
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,383
Abdullah Bin Jada'an(عبدالله بن جدعان) was a wealthy man in Makkah.

118
00:09:42,931 --> 00:09:44,518
And he freed Sohaib(صهيب).

119
00:09:45,221 --> 00:09:47,527
Sohaib(صهيب) was bright and intelligent and active.

120
00:09:47,908 --> 00:09:50,178
 So, he started the business and he acquired wealth.

121
00:09:50,851 --> 00:09:58,778
When he wanted to make Hijrah(هجرة), he covered his wealth, dig up hole for it and hide it somewhere and he left.

122
00:09:59,048 --> 00:10:01,540
 So, some of the men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) pursued him.

123
00:10:02,318 --> 00:10:10,262
And they told him, You came to us as a poverty stricken beggar.

124
00:10:10,965 --> 00:10:13,982
With us, you grew wealthy and acquired status.

125
00:10:14,379 --> 00:10:17,204
And now you wantto take yourself and your money away,

126
00:10:17,601 --> 00:10:20,734
 In the name of Allah, By Allah, we will not allow this to happen.

127
00:10:21,186 --> 00:10:22,742
You came to us broke.

128
00:10:23,361 --> 00:10:26,194
 And now you're wealthy, you want to take your wealth and leave us.

129
00:10:26,908 --> 00:10:33,308
So, Sohaib(صهيب) said what if I ransom myself and give you my Wealth, they said then we'll allow you to go.

130
00:10:34,075 --> 00:10:40,908
In another narration, when he saw them following him, he drew out 40 arrows,

131
00:10:41,392 --> 00:10:44,011
and he said, I'm gonna stick each one of these, in one of you.

132
00:10:44,787 --> 00:10:50,645
And after I run out of arrows, I'm going to draw out my sword and then you'll know that I am a man.

133
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:55,779
I have left money in this particular place, you can go and take it and let me go.

134
00:10:56,041 --> 00:10:58,057
And they agreed to let him leave.

135
00:10:58,939 --> 00:11:03,428
This story of Sohaib(صهيب) represents an immigrant, who went into Makkah.

136
00:11:03,509 --> 00:11:07,794
He was an immigrant, who went to Makkah, he was a foreigner, he settled there,

137
00:11:08,169 --> 00:11:11,159
he gained status and made money.

138
00:11:11,723 --> 00:11:15,362
But when he wanted to leave for the sake of Allah, they didn't allow him to leave.

139
00:11:15,965 --> 00:11:22,663
Probably Muslims living in the West can take heed, of the story of Sohaibرضي الله عنه.

140
00:11:24,222 --> 00:11:30,510
The Muhajireen(مهاجرين), who moved from Makkah to Madina, They were feeling homesick.

141
00:11:31,053 --> 00:11:33,687
And they wanted to go back to Makkah.

142
00:11:34,353 --> 00:11:38,510
Back it says that Bilal(بلال) used to say; May Allah curse Utba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة)

143
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:44,790
and Shaibah Bin Rabiyah(شيبة بن ربيعة) and Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف) who have driven us out of Makkah to this land of diseases.

144
00:11:45,690 --> 00:11:48,498
Madina had swampy land

145
00:11:49,268 --> 00:11:57,268
and because of this, you had a lot of Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) it was malaria or what kind of diseases, but they would catch a fever.

146
00:11:57,611 --> 00:11:59,459
And Madina was famous about this.

147
00:11:59,602 --> 00:12:01,475
People who would go there would catch a fever.

148
00:12:01,611 --> 00:12:07,552
Some scholars today say that it might have been malaria because of the stagnant water that was in these swamps.

149
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:15,539
So, Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said that my father and Bilal(بلال) and Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فهيره) catch this fever,

150
00:12:15,913 --> 00:12:17,208
So I went to visit them.

151
00:12:17,485 --> 00:12:19,165
So I said, Oh my father, How are you?

152
00:12:19,367 --> 00:12:22,375
And he didn't respond back, He was just reciting lines of poetry.

153
00:12:22,946 --> 00:12:25,943
She went to Bilal(بلال) and said; Bilal(بلال), How are you? Same thing.

154
00:12:26,253 --> 00:12:27,800
Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فهيره) same thing.

155
00:12:28,015 --> 00:12:30,348
Ayesha(عائشه) said these men don't know what they're saying.

156
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:36,724
And she went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him about what Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was saying and what Bilal(بلال) was saying,

157
00:12:37,171 --> 00:12:40,572
reciting these lines of poetry, I could read you some of them.

158
00:12:40,804 --> 00:12:43,034
What Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Bilal(بلال) were saying

159
00:12:44,147 --> 00:12:47,528
For example, Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه would say;

160
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:54,823
Every man might arise among his family, Yet his death be closer than his sandal fangs.

161
00:12:55,222 --> 00:12:59,468
So, he was talking about death, thinking that he might die because of this fever.

162
00:12:59,831 --> 00:13:07,749
While Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فهيره) was saying, I have found death before tasting it,

163
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:11,885
a coward has his demise right above him,

164
00:13:12,202 --> 00:13:18,179
Every man fights hard with all his power as a bull protects its skin with its horns.

165
00:13:19,742 --> 00:13:28,060
And Bilalرضي الله عنه would say O, how happy I would be to spend the night in a valley covered with fresh grass and verdure.

166
00:13:28,423 --> 00:13:32,774
Will I ever again descend to magenta waters or see Shamaan Tufail(شمان طفيل),

167
00:13:32,814 --> 00:13:35,368
Shamaan Tufail(شمان طفيل), are two mountains in Makkah.

168
00:13:35,635 --> 00:13:39,237
All of these men were homesick they wanted to go back to Makkah.

169
00:13:39,764 --> 00:13:44,650
Bilal(بلال) as I said was saying O Allah curse Utba Bin Rabiyah(عتبة بن ربيعة), Shaibah Bin Rabiyah(شيبة بن ربيعة)

170
00:13:44,675 --> 00:13:50,947
and Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(امية بن خلف) alike for them having forced us out into the land of pestilence.

171
00:13:52,596 --> 00:13:56,441
Now if you've experienced being a foreigner in a land.

172
00:13:56,790 --> 00:14:00,274
I'm not saying tourists, having a feeling of being a tourist is different,

173
00:14:00,314 --> 00:14:04,077
I am saying you're driven out of your home, you're forced out of your home

174
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:08,609
and you're living in a place that you didn't really choose to go to.

175
00:14:08,934 --> 00:14:11,829
You were forced to go there, it's a horrible feeling.

176
00:14:12,218 --> 00:14:19,812
And add to that you become sick and your family are not around and there's nobody to take care of you.

177
00:14:20,082 --> 00:14:23,534
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was feeling very sorry for the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

178
00:14:23,924 --> 00:14:29,672
And when Ayesha(عائشه) came to her husband, Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him about the condition of Bilal(بلال)

179
00:14:29,749 --> 00:14:32,114
and Aamir Bin Fuhairah(عامربن فهيره) and her father Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

180
00:14:32,352 --> 00:14:34,852
 Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

181
00:14:34,979 --> 00:14:38,565
اَللَّهُمَّ حَبِّبْ إلَيْنَا الْمَدِيْنَّهْ كَحُبِّنَا مَكَهْ اَوْ اَشَدْ،

182
00:14:38,771 --> 00:14:44,147
