352
00:29:04,965 --> 00:29:13,481
It was a test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ for the Jews, who said, he has left the Qibla(قبله) of the Ambiyaa(أنبياء), before him.

353
00:29:14,981 --> 00:29:18,975
And that shows you that Muhammadﷺ is not a prophet of Allah,

354
00:29:19,292 --> 00:29:21,964
they consider that Jerusalem was the Qibla(قبله) of the Ambiyaa(أنبياء).

355
00:29:22,606 --> 00:29:24,931
And it was a test for the believers,

356
00:29:25,614 --> 00:29:31,585
to see if they would stand firm on the orders of Rasool Allah ﷺ and change the Qibla(قبله) with him or not.

357
00:29:32,302 --> 00:29:35,841
So, it was a trial from Allahعَزّوجَلّ for all of these four groups.

358
00:29:36,373 --> 00:29:38,698
We'll recite some of the Ayaat(آيات) revealed.

359
00:29:39,818 --> 00:29:46,942
The foolish among the people will say, what has turned them away from their Qibla(قبله), which they used to face.

360
00:29:47,267 --> 00:29:53,326
And Al-Bara'a Bin Aazib(ألبرآء بن عازب) in an authentic narration says that the foolish among the people, refers to Al-Yahood(أليهود).

361
00:29:53,992 --> 00:30:04,070
سَيَقُولُ السُّفَهَاءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ مَا وَلَّاهُمْ عَنْ قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِي كَانُوا عَلَيْهَا ۚ

362
00:30:04,689 --> 00:30:08,160
قُلْ لِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ ۚ

363
00:30:08,478 --> 00:30:15,136
يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ إِلَىٰ صِرَاطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ۝

364
00:30:16,267 --> 00:30:22,614
The foolish among the people will say, what has turned them away from their Qibla(قبله), which they used to face.

365
00:30:22,904 --> 00:30:28,730
Say, to Allah belongs the east and the west, He guides whom, He wills to a straight path.

366
00:30:29,490 --> 00:30:34,604
Who's the One, Who created Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), Makkah, Who was the One, Who created Jerusalem?

367
00:30:35,082 --> 00:30:36,599
It all belongs to Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

368
00:30:36,663 --> 00:30:42,922
to Allah belongs the east and the west, therefore, it is up to Allahعَزّوجَلّ to choose which Qibla(قبله) you face.

369
00:30:43,279 --> 00:30:44,406
Everything belongs to Him.

370
00:30:44,446 --> 00:30:46,755
So, He has the authority to tell you, where to pray.

371
00:30:47,816 --> 00:30:50,983
Because, the Jews were saying, Allah cannot change His mind,

372
00:30:52,090 --> 00:30:55,842
Either the first Qibla(قبله) was right or the second Qibla(قبله) was right,

373
00:30:55,882 --> 00:30:59,215
if the first Qibla(قبله) was right, then your prayers now, are not accepted.

374
00:30:59,587 --> 00:31:04,374
And if the second Qibla(قبله) is right, then your old prayers are not accepted.

375
00:31:05,503 --> 00:31:07,158
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ respond by this Ayah(آية).

376
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:08,745
And then the next Ayah(آية) says

377
00:31:09,084 --> 00:31:19,986
وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ

378
00:31:20,462 --> 00:31:30,145
لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا ۗ

379
00:31:31,101 --> 00:31:35,929
And thus, We have made you a median community, Umaat-U-Wasat( أمة وسط)

380
00:31:36,373 --> 00:31:39,294
that you will be witnesses over the people

381
00:31:39,590 --> 00:31:42,326
and the messenger will be a witness over you.

382
00:31:42,794 --> 00:31:45,016
So, Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر)  comments on this and says;

383
00:31:45,072 --> 00:31:50,812
likewise we have made you the best of nations, the very essence of the world,

384
00:31:51,239 --> 00:31:56,628
The most noble of all groups, the most honorable of the ancient and the high born,

385
00:31:56,995 --> 00:32:02,477
so that you may be witnesses on Judgment Day against those, who have combined against you.

386
00:32:02,787 --> 00:32:08,519
And so that they may give testimony, On that day, to your great virtue.

387
00:32:09,503 --> 00:32:10,645
Then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

388
00:32:10,837 --> 00:32:24,393
وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الْقِبْلَةَ الَّتِي كُنْتَ عَلَيْهَا إِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الرَّسُولَ مِمَّنْ يَنْقَلِبُ عَلَىٰ عَقِبَيْهِ ۚ

389
00:32:25,091 --> 00:32:31,599
وَإِنْ كَانَتْ لَكَبِيرَةً إِلَّا عَلَى الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ ۗ

390
00:32:32,047 --> 00:32:36,354
And we did not make the Qibla(قبله), which you used to face,

391
00:32:36,695 --> 00:32:43,113
except that we might make evident, who would follow the messenger, from who would turn back on his heels.

392
00:32:43,224 --> 00:32:44,105
So, it was a test.

393
00:32:45,033 --> 00:32:50,509
And Indeed, it is difficult except for those whom Allah has guided, it was difficult to change the Qibla(قبله).

394
00:32:51,375 --> 00:32:53,677
But it was easy for the ones whom Allah has guided,

395
00:32:53,923 --> 00:32:57,034
 and never would Allah have caused you to lose your faith.

396
00:32:57,288 --> 00:33:00,947
See, because the Jews said, what about the Muslims who died facing the old Qibla(قبله),

397
00:33:01,114 --> 00:33:03,170
that means all of their efforts is wasted.

398
00:33:03,614 --> 00:33:04,813
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says,

399
00:33:05,279 --> 00:33:14,223
وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ لِيُضِيعَ إِيمَانَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

400
00:33:15,059 --> 00:33:20,825
Allah will not waste your efforts, indeed Allah is to the people kind and merciful.

401
00:33:21,913 --> 00:33:27,753
قَدْ نَرَىٰ تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ ۖ

402
00:33:28,356 --> 00:33:33,206
فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضَاهَا ۚ

403
00:33:33,658 --> 00:33:37,577
فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ

404
00:33:37,982 --> 00:33:42,958
وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ ۗ

405
00:33:43,554 --> 00:33:51,071
وَإِنَّ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ لَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ ۗ

406
00:33:51,563 --> 00:33:56,969
وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ۝

407
00:33:58,493 --> 00:34:06,233
وَلَئِنْ أَتَيْتَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ بِكُلِّ آيَةٍ مَا تَبِعُوا قِبْلَتَكَ ۚ

408
00:34:06,963 --> 00:34:12,619
وَمَا أَنْتَ بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَتَهُمْ ۚ

409
00:34:12,905 --> 00:34:17,532
وَمَا بَعْضُهُمْ بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَةَ بَعْضٍ ۚ

410
00:34:17,945 --> 00:34:31,218
وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ أَهْوَاءَهُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا جَاءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ ۙ إِنَّكَ إِذًا لَمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ۝

411
00:34:32,337 --> 00:34:36,972
We have certainly seen the turning of your face O Muhammad(محمد) towards the heavens,

412
00:34:37,156 --> 00:34:39,948
تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ ۖ

413
00:34:39,987 --> 00:34:41,170
he wanted the Qibla(قبله) to change,

414
00:34:41,547 --> 00:34:46,117
and we will surely turn you to a Qibla(قبله), with which you will be pleased.

415
00:34:46,562 --> 00:34:49,339
So, turn your face towards Al-Masjid Al-Haraam(المسجدالحرام)

416
00:34:49,667 --> 00:34:52,944
and wherever you are, turn your faces towards it.

417
00:34:53,944 --> 00:35:03,327
Indeed, those who have been given the Scripture will know that it is the truth from their Lord and Allah is not unaware of what they do.

418
00:35:03,956 --> 00:35:07,398
And If you brought to those who are given the Scripture, every sign,

419
00:35:07,612 --> 00:35:11,880
they would not follow your Qibla(قبله), nor will you be a follower of their Qibla(قبله),

420
00:35:12,052 --> 00:35:15,062
nor would they be followers of one another's Qibla(قبله).

421
00:35:15,261 --> 00:35:20,230
So, If you were to follow their desires, after what has come to you of knowledge,

422
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:23,611
indeed you would then be among the wrong doers.

423
00:35:23,849 --> 00:35:29,615
Anybody who follows the People of the Book today, after he has already known the truth,

424
00:35:29,964 --> 00:35:32,512
He will be among the wrongdoers.

425
00:35:33,433 --> 00:35:34,512
 Then Allah says,

426
00:35:35,524 --> 00:35:39,184
those to whom we gave the scripture know him, Muhammad(محمد),

427
00:35:39,309 --> 00:35:44,920
as they know their own sons, but indeed a party of them conceal the truth, while they know it.

428
00:35:45,249 --> 00:35:48,883
The truth is from your Lord, so never be among the doubters.

429
00:35:49,439 --> 00:35:54,111
For each religious following is a prayer direction toward which it faces.

430
00:35:54,420 --> 00:36:01,261
So raise to all that is good, wherever you may be, Allah will bring you forth for judgment all together.

431
00:36:01,515 --> 00:36:04,197
Indeed Allah is over all things competent.

432
00:36:04,481 --> 00:36:14,219
الَّذِينَ آتَيْنَاهُمُ الْكِتَابَ يَعْرِفُونَهُ كَمَا يَعْرِفُونَ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ ۖ

433
00:36:14,750 --> 00:36:22,298
وَإِنَّ فَرِيقًا مِنْهُمْ لَيَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ۝

434
00:36:23,433 --> 00:36:28,965
الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ ۖ فَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ۝

435
00:36:29,767 --> 00:36:34,064
وَلِكُلٍّ وِجْهَةٌ هُوَ مُوَلِّيهَا ۖ

436
00:36:34,247 --> 00:36:37,009
فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرَاتِ ۚ

437
00:36:37,572 --> 00:36:42,597
أَيْنَ مَا تَكُونُوا يَأْتِ بِكُمُ اللَّهُ جَمِيعًا ۚ

438
00:36:43,001 --> 00:36:48,714
إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ۝

439
00:36:49,601 --> 00:36:55,298
وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۖ

440
00:36:55,925 --> 00:37:04,165
وَإِنَّهُ لَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ ۗ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ۝

441
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:10,835
وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ

442
00:37:11,271 --> 00:37:16,424
وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ

443
00:37:16,869 --> 00:37:24,668
لِئَلَّا يَكُونَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَيْكُمْ حُجَّةٌ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا مِنْهُمْ

444
00:37:25,156 --> 00:37:34,125
فَلَا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَاخْشَوْنِي وَلِأُتِمَّ نِعْمَتِي عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ۝

445
00:37:35,162 --> 00:37:40,753
So, from wherever you go out for prayer, O Muhammad(محمد), Turn your face toward Al-Masjid Al-Haraam(المسجدالحرام)

446
00:37:41,113 --> 00:37:43,613
And Indeed, it is the truth from your Lord.

447
00:37:43,882 --> 00:37:46,367
And Allah is not unaware of what you do.

448
00:37:46,740 --> 00:37:51,351
And from wherever you go out for prayer, Turn your face towards Al-Masjid Al-Haraam(المسجد الحرام),

449
00:37:51,444 --> 00:37:52,932
 it is repeating the order again.

450
00:37:53,151 --> 00:37:56,984
And wherever you believers may be turn your faces toward it,

451
00:37:57,326 --> 00:38:01,241
in order that the people will not have any argument against you.

452
00:38:01,543 --> 00:38:06,495
 Except for those of them who commit wrong, so fear them not but fear Me.

453
00:38:06,709 --> 00:38:08,265
This is an important concept here.

454
00:38:08,805 --> 00:38:13,405
People might blame you for doing some things which are Islamic, which you know, are the truth.

455
00:38:13,852 --> 00:38:17,827
In every age and time people pick on some things in Islam.

456
00:38:18,136 --> 00:38:21,081
You know, in one age, they're going to say, Well, Islam is oppression to women,

457
00:38:21,208 --> 00:38:26,158
in another age, they will say, Islam is giving too much rights for women.

458
00:38:26,505 --> 00:38:31,697
It changes in one point of time that people will say, Islam is religion of violence.

459
00:38:31,999 --> 00:38:33,950
Islam is this, Islam is that,

460
00:38:34,053 --> 00:38:37,244
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling you, fear them not but fear Me.

461
00:38:37,566 --> 00:38:40,879
Do what Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants from you, that is what counts,

462
00:38:41,077 --> 00:38:44,568
do what Allah wants from you and forget about what the people are going to say.

463
00:38:45,011 --> 00:38:53,420
So, fear them not but fear Me, and it is so, I may complete My favor upon you and that you may be guided.

464
00:38:53,476 --> 00:38:57,159
 Every new order that comes from Allah is a favor from Allah.

465
00:38:58,894 --> 00:39:04,501
This was the incident of the changing of Al-Qibla(ألقبله), which was very controversial in its time,

466
00:39:04,739 --> 00:39:07,454
and it was a test, it was a test for all the people,

467
00:39:07,655 --> 00:39:12,904
just as you know everything else is a test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ to see if we will pass or fail,

468
00:39:12,991 --> 00:39:17,285
if we will accept it or not how strong is our faith in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

469
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:23,727
Rasool Allah ﷺ was developing the economical system of the new Islamic state,

470
00:39:23,838 --> 00:39:29,427
so he designated an area next to Al-Masjid Al-Nabawi(المسجدالنبوي) to be the Madina marketplace,

471
00:39:29,609 --> 00:39:32,085
the central market of Madina.

472
00:39:32,268 --> 00:39:36,858
Rasool Allah ﷺ devoted this space to be a market and he said;

473
00:39:37,144 --> 00:39:42,858
  هَذَا سُوْقُكُمْ فَلَاِ ينتقصن وَلَا يُضْرَبَنَّ عَلَيْهِ خَرَاجْ

474
00:39:43,185 --> 00:39:45,061
This is your marketplace.

475
00:39:45,347 --> 00:39:46,252
So

476
00:39:46,847 --> 00:39:48,483
  وَلَا يُضْرَبَنَّ عَلَيْهِ خَرَاجْ

477
00:39:48,523 --> 00:39:53,521
if I'm going to translate it, it's going to mean, no taxes should be levied on it.

478
00:39:53,871 --> 00:40:01,909
So, it was a tax free market, because Kharaaj(خراج) is money that is taken by the government on the merchandise.

479
00:40:02,649 --> 00:40:08,375
So, it was a tax free market, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to fix any prices.

480
00:40:08,685 --> 00:40:11,494
Once the prices were skyrocketing.

481
00:40:11,862 --> 00:40:17,796
So the Sahabah came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said; We want you to fix the prices, the items are becoming very expensive.

482
00:40:18,038 --> 00:40:19,195
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

483
00:40:19,409 --> 00:40:20,818
 اِنَّ الله هوَ الْمُسَعرْ

484
00:40:20,993 --> 00:40:24,381
Allah is the One, Who sets the prices, I don't want to interfere.

485
00:40:24,698 --> 00:40:26,258
It was a supply and demand thing.

486
00:40:26,534 --> 00:40:29,555
According to the supply and demand, the prices will go up and down,

487
00:40:29,580 --> 00:40:34,141
Allah is the one who gives Rizq(رزق) and Allah is the one who set the prices, I'm not going to involve in that.

488
00:40:34,423 --> 00:40:40,359
So, this shows you the freedom that Islam has given to the Islamic economical system,

489
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:48,142
that does not place restrictions on the flow of money and how people would buy and sell in their trade.

490
00:40:48,741 --> 00:40:53,350
Finally, the ruling of fasting, was in the second year of Hijrah(هجرة),

491
00:40:53,390 --> 00:40:56,636
now we're getting into the second year of Hijrah(هجرة), events that happen then.

492
00:40:56,874 --> 00:40:59,572
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية) Surat Ul Bakarah(سورة البقرة).

493
00:40:59,715 --> 00:41:13,238
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ۝

494
00:41:13,920 --> 00:41:21,091
O, you who have believed decreed upon you is fasting, as it was decreed upon those before you,

495
00:41:21,377 --> 00:41:23,412
that you might become righteous.

496
00:41:23,678 --> 00:41:26,655
So, the purpose or the wisdom behind, fasting is Taqwaa(تقوى).

497
00:41:26,980 --> 00:41:29,817
So, that you may become righteous.

498
00:41:32,539 --> 00:41:34,435
We're still within the first two years of Hijrah(هجرة).

499
00:41:34,475 --> 00:41:38,086
We're talking about events that happened during that time span.

500
00:41:38,911 --> 00:41:43,135
Rasool Allah ﷺ, also married Ayeshaرضي الله عنها during that time,

501
00:41:43,575 --> 00:41:49,300
or actually I should say the consummation of the marriage to Ayesha(عائشه) occurred in that time.

502
00:41:49,578 --> 00:41:57,255
